---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../components/TrustStrip.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import { business } from '../lib/business';
import { href, routes } from '../lib/links';
import { breadcrumbSchema, localBusinessSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const { identity, credentials } = business;
---

<Site
  title="About Stonelane Renovations"
  description={identity.positioning}
  schema={[
    localBusinessSchema(),
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <header class="grid-editorial section--tight">
    <div class="col-half">
      <p class="section__eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">We price the job properly, then hold the price</h1>
      <p class="section__lede">{identity.differentiatorLong}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-half-end">
      <Figure
        id="team-group"
        alt="The Stonelane team outside the Northmead workshop"
        priority
        sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 45vw, 92vw"
      />
    </div>
  </header>

  <TrustStrip />

  <section class="grid-editorial section" aria-labelledby="how">
    <div class="col-text">
      <h2 id="how" class="section__title">How a fixed price is actually possible</h2>
      <p class="beat-body">
        Most renovation quotes carry provisional sums and allowances — a number pencilled in
        for something nobody has looked at yet. When the walls open up, the number moves, and
        it only ever moves one way. The industry treats this as normal.
      </p>
      <p class="beat-body">
        It is normal because investigating properly costs money before anyone has signed
        anything. We do it anyway: we test for asbestos before we price rather than after, we
        put an engineer on the footings before quoting a second storey, and we open up behind
        the appliances in any house built before 1990. It means we quote later than other
        builders. It also means the number we quote is the number you pay.
      </p>
      <p class="beat-body">
        When something genuinely unforeseeable turns up — rock two metres above where the
        geotechnical report put it — we carry it. That is what the price is for.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-aside">
      <Figure
        id="home-differentiator"
        alt="A fixed price quote on a site table beside a tape measure and a pencil"
        sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 30vw, 92vw"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid-editorial section section--ruled" aria-labelledby="houses">
    <div class="col-text">
      <h2 id="houses" class="section__title">The houses we work on</h2>
      <p class="beat-body">{identity.positioning}</p>
      <p class="beat-body">
        That is a narrower brief than most builders advertise, and deliberately so. Brick
        veneer, weatherboard, fibro and project homes from the 1960s to the 1990s have a
        predictable set of problems — original wiring at end of life, galvanised pipe,
        asbestos in the eaves, concrete tile roofs with a decade left, slabs that were never
        tied together. Knowing that stock well is what lets us price it without guessing.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-aside">
      <Figure
        id="about-workshop-detail"
        alt="The selections sample wall in the Northmead workshop"
        sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 30vw, 92vw"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid-editorial section section--ruled" aria-labelledby="credentials">
    <div class="col-text">
      <h2 id="credentials" class="section__title">Licensing and cover</h2>
      <p class="beat-body">
        Everything here can be checked, and the licence links to the public register so you can
        check it in one click. We would rather you did.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="col-wide creds">
      <div class="cred">
        <dt>{credentials.licence.label}</dt>
        <dd>
          <a href={credentials.licence.verifyUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
            {credentials.licence.number}
          </a>
          <span class="cred__note">Held by {credentials.licence.holder}</span>
        </dd>
      </div>
      {
        credentials.insurance.map((i) => (
          <div class="cred">
            <dt>{i.name}</dt>
            <dd>
              {i.detail}
              {i.note && <span class="cred__note">{i.note}</span>}
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      {
        credentials.memberships.map((m) => (
          <div class="cred">
            <dt>{m.name}</dt>
            <dd>
              Member {m.memberNumber}
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <div class="cred">
        <dt>Warranty</dt>
        <dd>{credentials.warranty.summary}</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="grid-editorial section section--ruled" aria-labelledby="not">
    <div class="col-text">
      <h2 id="not" class="section__title">What we are not</h2>
      <p class="beat-body">
        We are not the right builder for a single bathroom swap with no layout change, or a
        kitchen where the existing layout is being kept. Under
        {' '}<a href={href(routes.costs)}>our minimum</a>, a specialist trade working directly
        will cost you less and happen sooner, and we will tell you that on the first call
        rather than after a site visit.
      </p>
      <p class="beat-body">
        We are also not a design practice. We do design and construct under one contract
        because it removes the gap where responsibility usually gets lost — but if you want a
        distinguished piece of architecture, engage an architect and we will happily build it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CallToAction />
</Site>

<style>
  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-display-m);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin-block: var(--space-2xs) var(--space-s);
  }

  .beat-body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .beat-body + .beat-body {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
  }

  .creds {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(17rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-m) var(--space-s);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
  }

  .cred {
    padding-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
    border-block-start: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .cred dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-display);
    font-size: var(--text-title-s);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.014em;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3xs);
  }

  .cred dd {
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .cred__note {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3xs);
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
</style>
